{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-xy+{y}^{2})=2x-y, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-xy+{y}^{2})=-x+2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x-y & -x+2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389396 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389396 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389396 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389399 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389396 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389400 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389396 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389396 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389396 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389396 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186389401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389396 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9f5c60e8-8aeb-55da-b9fb-b42572387a77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389397 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}2x-1 & 2y-1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389397 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417]